{
 "_readme": "The chord ladder for every chord game (home Chord Practice and Boss Battle, and the classroom rig's chord games), easiest to hardest. A chord is a root note plus a type (Em, Bb7, F#m7...). The first tier is the Band Skills Ladder (Dave and Simone's): its order and its shapes come from the ladder's Chord charts tab, so G and C are the two-finger shapes and F is the Fmaj7 shape. Ask Claude to 'update the games from the ladder' after changing it there. A student unlocks chords in this order, one at a time.",
 "_shapes_readme": "One guitar shape per chord, six strings low E to high e: 'o' open, 'x' not played, or 'fret:finger' (fingers 1 index, 2 middle, 3 ring, 4 pinky). Guitar games show this as the chord diagram AND listen for exactly the notes this shape sounds (so the two-finger G's open E counts as part of the chord). Piano uses the plain chord type instead. ladderShapes lists the chords whose shape came from the ladder; the rest are standard shapes.",
