 "_piano_readme": "Piano players climb their own ladder (Chord Quest and Boss Battle on piano). Like guitar's Easy-G and Easy-C, the first four chords are simpler: TWO-NOTE chords (pianoEasy: the root and the 3rd, so C is C+E and Am is A+C), labelled Easy-C etc. Playing the full chord still counts. The next shelf is the same four as full chords (C:3 = full C), then the rest. Full chords show fingers 1-2-4 (Dave, 13 Oct: 1-3-5 is too much of a stretch for little hands); four-note chords 1-2-3-5. Same chord names as guitar, so the same songs open up; once a full chord is won, songs use it.",
